(6140785, 903513, 120160, '<td valign="top">Once again thanks to all for the wonderful welcome =)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scarbrd:</b></div><hr/><i> Great, ANOTHER member of the Singapore DPC ribbon hogs! Great shot! I see you hang out with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=79955" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">AndrewT</a>, watch out, he''s a trouble maker. So is that <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=86336" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Soon</a> character! ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Haha.. If AndrewT is a trouble maker, then watch out.. I''m ''trouble''.. I just started like a month ago and he is the one who ''make'' me. Wouldn''t have gonna this shot without his guidance.. =) <br/> <br/></td>', 'Once again thanks to all for the wonderful welcome =) Originally posted by scarbrd: Great, ANOTHER member of the Singapore DPC ribbon hogs! Great shot! I see you hang out with  AndrewT, watch out, he''s a trouble maker. So is that  Soon character! ;-)   Haha.. If AndrewT is a trouble maker, then watch out.. I''m ''trouble''.. I just started like a month ago and he is the one who ''make'' me. Wouldn''t have gonna this shot without his guidance.. =)  ', '2010-08-25 12:48:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140786, 904170, 104230, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, Wendy.  Lovely lighting, great shot.</td>', 'Congratulations, Wendy.  Lovely lighting, great shot.', '2010-08-25 12:50:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140804, 904134, 110792, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I came up with the oxymoron idea and created the poster. I have this nice brick wall in my house and it was perfect for this shot. Picked a photo of a cat, printed the poster, stuck it to the wall and took the shot. Processing was all done in Lightroom, playing with contrast, saturation, exposure, etc.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I came up with the oxymoron idea and created the poster. I have this nice brick wall in my house and it was perfect for this shot. Picked a photo of a cat, printed the poster, stuck it to the wall and took the shot. Processing was all done in Lightroom, playing with contrast, saturation, exposure, etc.', '2010-08-25 13:11:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140818, 903864, 63244, '<td valign="top">What a fun shot!! ''grats on the blue with this. Nicely done.</td>', 'What a fun shot!! ''grats on the blue with this. Nicely done.', '2010-08-25 13:31:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6140823, 904102, 5885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AmelieDeSade:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Magnum_za:</b></div><hr/><i> Well Done.<br/>But you got 8 x 2, 5 x 3 and 15 x 4 Voters for the "tsk tsk OMG it''s a Gun who gives a ---- for the photography" crowd :(<br/>PS: You left out a description of the most important prop ;) Looks like a DA 9mm but which one, there are thousands. Either that or its a MIC Toy. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, that is a Ruger .40S&amp;W, the P91DC, to be precise. Not only is it my favorite, its the most accurate I own. Just to clarify. =D </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL... and that''s the final answer :)</td>', 'Originally posted by AmelieDeSade: Originally posted by Magnum_za: Well Done.But you got 8 x 2, 5 x 3 and 15 x 4 Voters for the "tsk tsk OMG it''s a Gun who gives a ---- for the photography" crowd :(PS: You left out a description of the most important prop ;) Looks like a DA 9mm but which one, there are thousands. Either that or its a MIC Toy.   Actually, that is a Ruger .40S&W, the P91DC, to be precise. Not only is it my favorite, its the most accurate I own. Just to clarify. =D   LOL... and that''s the final answer :)', '2010-08-25 13:40:33.000000', NULL, 0),
